   "source": {
    "label": "the:worst",
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "Given a time horizon $T$, a stream of $K$ arms, and $1 \\leq B \\leq \\log\\log T$ passes over this stream, consider any algorithm $\\mathcal{A}$ that only store $o(K/B)$ arms in memory, we have $\\textnormal{Regret}(\\mathcal{A}) = \\Omega ( (TB)^{\\frac{2^B}{2^{B+1}-1}} K^{\\frac{2^B-1}{2^{B+1}-1}})$ in expectation for some problem instances."
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Regret defined as sum_t (mu* - mu_{x_t}); in expectation -> pseudo-regret. Proof sketch is informal. Special cases: B=1 gives Omega(K^{1/3}T^{2/3}); B=loglogT gives Omega(sqrt(KT loglogT))."
  },
